<title>FRANCE: EU proposes new taxes on fuels.</title>
<headline>EU proposes new taxes on fuels.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission proposed Wednesday a series of new taxes on motor and heating oils, electricity and gas.</p>
<p>The proposal was called for by European Union governments to compensate for a failure to agree a carbon dioxide tax in the early 1990's to cut harmful emissions.  </p>
<p>European Commissioner Mario Monti, responsible for taxation, stressed at a news conference that the tax should not increase the bloc's overall tax burden, saying that national governments should use any new revenue to cut labour-related costs.</p>
<p>&quot;This is not meant to be a new tax,&quot; he said, in a move aimed at smoothing industry concerns.</p>
<p>The purpose of the tax is to bring EU national tax rates closer together to avoid competition and to help the environment.</p>
<p>The proposal must go to EU ministers for approval.</p>
</text>
